From a352fca149b47b438f4cf4370fafbf80e0775528 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Konsta=20Alaj=C3=A4rvi?= <konsta.alajarvi@qt.io>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 14:48:20 +0300
Subject: Android: guard QtLoader against UnsatisfiedLinkError

When Qt libraries are loaded on a device ABI not
present in the AAR, System.loadLibrary() throws
UnsatisfiedLinkError. Since UnsatisfiedLinkError is not
explicitly caught, it escapes the existing catch block
in loadLibraryHelper(), crashing the process.

Add a UnsatisfiedLinkError catch in loadLibraryHelper()
so the failure is logged and null returned, allowing
loadQtLibraries() to produce LoadingResult.Failed and
QtServiceBase.onCreate() to call stopSelf() instead of
crashing.

Add a warning log to resolvePreferredAbi() when the app
does not ship with any of the ABIs that the device supports.

Guard QtServiceBase.onDestroy() with an isStarted check
before calling terminateQtNativeApplication(). Otherwise,
calling JNI method terminateQtNativeApplication() when
native libraries are not loaded results in another
UnsatisfiedLinkError crash.

While at it, drop a stray word from the documentation of
getApkNativeLibrariesDir().

Fixes: QTBUG-141461
Pick-to: 6.12 6.11 6.8
Done-with: Assam Boudjelthia <assam.boudjelthia@qt.io>
Change-Id: If33268d027b10c1a3486ae4b4bafcdded5aee9f1
Reviewed-by: Ville Voutilainen <ville.voutilainen@qt.io>
(Cherry-picked from commit 5d3d18fa6d4f65dbce326b149f97bb7ce458e18c)
